6. CLI entrypoints (pyproject scripts, scripts/*.py|*.sh, Makefile targets) superseded or never invoked by anything;
7. web app pages/components that are unreachable (no route/link navigation) — spot-check web/app directory routing;
8. build/package/deploy surfaces (Makefile targets, docker/ images, compose files, infra/helm charts) with no downstream consumer — note: some helm/compose files may be incubating infrastructure; verify references before reporting;
9. LLM/AI surface: agent tools or council roles defined but never dispatched, prompt packs never loaded.
10. Workflow/CI: note that Large-Model-Application/.github/workflows is NOT registered by GitHub (only repo-root .github/workflows counts) — check whether that nested ci.yml contains gates that therefore never run (this is documented known state; classify accordingly).

Known context to avoid false positives: predictive_maintenance/wireless_rul.py was deliberately retired; knowledge double-bridge (S8) is intentionally not started; docs claim edge uplink + wireless-events endpoints ARE consumed by the C++ edge; the platform has a lot of staging/GPU/infra code that may be legitimate but possibly unreferenced — verify before claiming.

For EACH finding provide: exact path + symbol/file:line; the exact grep scope proving absence of a consumer; classification (no caller | test-only caller | dead dispatch | parsed-never-read | superseded-entrypoint | unreachable-artifact); verification it's real production code. Then severity (Critical/Important/Minor), concrete consequence, and ONE disposition: remove | replan with a real consumer | document as intentional incubation (with exit condition).

Only report verified findings; do not pad. 5-20 high-confidence findings expected. End with a "candidates checked and cleared" list.

